BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:223700@caiso.com
DTSTART:20260319T160000Z
DTEND:20260319T180000Z
SUMMARY:Training - Scheduling Infrastructure and Business Rules (SIBR) Advanced Bid Submission and Validation
DESCRIPTION:What topics will be covered?   \nThis session will provide more in-depth information about the Scheduling Infrastructure and Business Rules (SIBR) application by reviewing several complex bid-submission scenarios, including Transfer System Resources (TSRs) Types 1–4, transient TSRs, contract reference numbers, and transfer-capacity limits. It will also guide users step-by-step through resolving common errors.\nWho should attend?\nThe primary audience for this training is SIBR UI users. Specifically, staff from entities who are responsible for submitting or validating economic bids and self-schedules in the Day-Ahead Market, whether through SIBR or their own third-party software.\nWeb and audio participation information\nRegistration is required for this training session - \nhttps://caiso.regfox.com/training-scheduling-infrastructure-and-business-rules-sibr-advanced-bid-submission--validation-\nYou will receive Webex login information in a confirmation email.\nRelated information\nThe session will be recorded and posted to the ISO Training center, Western Energy Markets webpage a few days after the event.\n\nPlease contact CustomerReadiness@caiso.com with questions about this session. \n\nView more information on this event and its related documents: https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/training-scheduling-infrastructure-and-business-rules-sibr-advanced-bid-submission-and-validation-mar-19-2026-0900-am
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body lang="EN-US" link="#0072BC" vlink="#03519A" style="font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;" ><div><p style="margin-left:0in;"><strong>What topics will be covered?     </strong></p><p style="margin-left:0in;">This session will provide more in-depth information about the Scheduling Infrastructure and Business Rules (SIBR) application by reviewing several complex bid-submission scenarios, including Transfer System Resources (TSRs) Types 1–4, transient TSRs, contract reference numbers, and transfer-capacity limits. It will also guide users step-by-step through resolving common errors.</p><p style="margin-left:0in;"><strong>Who should attend?</strong></p><p style="margin-left:0in;">The primary audience for this training is SIBR UI users. Specifically, staff from entities who are responsible for submitting or validating economic bids and self-schedules in the Day-Ahead Market, whether through SIBR or their own third-party software.</p><p style="margin-left:0in;"><strong>Web and audio participation information</strong></p><p style="margin-left:0in;">Registration is required for this training session -  </p><p><a target="_blank" href="https://caiso.regfox.com/training-scheduling-infrastructure-and-business-rules-sibr-advanced-bid-submission--validation-" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://caiso.regfox.com/training-scheduling-infrastructure-and-business-rules-sibr-advanced-bid-submission--validation-</a></p><p style="margin-left:0in;">You will receive Webex login information in a confirmation email.</p><p><strong>Related information</strong></p><p style="margin-left:0in;">The session will be recorded and posted to the <a target="_blank" href="https://www.caiso.com/stakeholder/training/western-energy-markets" rel="noreferrer noopener">ISO Training center, Western Energy Markets webpage</a> a few days after the event.</p></div><div><p>Please contact <a href="mailto:CustomerReadiness@caiso.com">CustomerReadiness@caiso.com</a> with questions about this session.  </p></div><div><p><a href="https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/training-scheduling-infrastructure-and-business-rules-sibr-advanced-bid-submission-and-validation-mar-19-2026-0900-am" target="_blank">View more information on this event and its related documents.</a></p></div></body></html>
URL:https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/training-scheduling-infrastructure-and-business-rules-sibr-advanced-bid-submission-and-validation-mar-19-2026-0900-am
DTSTAMP:20260218T180000Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:219777@caiso.com
DTSTART:20260317T200000Z
DTEND:20260317T210000Z
SUMMARY:Tentative: Interconnection Customer User Group
DESCRIPTION:NOTE: Do not add to personal calendar. Meeting date and details to be confirmed in a future notice. \nThe Interconnection Customer User Group bi-weekly call provides an opportunity for CAISO interconnection customers to discuss industry questions and concerns regarding infrastructure policies and processes, including transmission planning and development, interconnection, deliverability, and contracting. This group will meet every other Tuesday from 1:00-2:00p.m.\nWhat topics will be covered?\nAgendas will generally be industry-driven.Topic suggestions are due by close of business on the Wednesday prior to the meeting to ykopylovalford@caiso.com or ISOStakeholderAffairs@caiso.com.A high-level agenda will be posted here by close of business the day prior to the meeting.Who should attend?\nThis call is open only to CAISO Interconnection Customers and state agency representatives.Attendees must pre-register for the recurring meeting here.Registration is required for this meeting - Interconnection Customer User Group Registration Link\nNotice - https://www.caiso.com/notices/interconnection-customer-user-group-call-3-18-25 \n\nYelena Kopylov-alford, ykopylovalford@caiso.com \n\nView more information on this event and its related documents: https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/interconnection-customer-user-group-mar-17-2026-0100-pm
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body lang="EN-US" link="#0072BC" vlink="#03519A" style="font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;" ><div><p><i><strong>NOTE: Do not add to personal calendar. Meeting date and details to be confirmed in a future notice.  </strong></i></p><p style="margin-left:0in;">The Interconnection Customer User Group bi-weekly call provides an opportunity for CAISO interconnection customers to discuss industry questions and concerns regarding infrastructure policies and processes, including transmission planning and development, interconnection, deliverability, and contracting. This group will meet every other Tuesday from 1:00-2:00p.m.</p><p style="margin-left:0in;"><strong>What topics will be covered?</strong></p><ul style="list-style-type:disc;"><li>Agendas will generally be industry-driven.</li><li>Topic suggestions are due by close of business on the Wednesday prior to the meeting to <a href="mailto:ykopylovalford@caiso.com">ykopylovalford@caiso.com</a> or <a href="mailto:ISOStakeholderAffairs@caiso.com">ISOStakeholderAffairs@caiso.com</a>.</li><li>A high-level agenda will be posted here by close of business the day prior to the meeting.</li></ul><p style="margin-left:0in;"><strong>Who should attend?</strong></p><ul style="list-style-type:disc;"><li>This call is open only to CAISO Interconnection Customers and state agency representatives.</li><li>Attendees must pre-register for the recurring meeting <a target="_blank" href="https://caiso.regfox.com/interconnection-customer-user-group-march-18-2025" rel="noreferrer noopener">here</a>.</li></ul><p><i><strong>Registration is required for this meeting - </strong></i><a target="_blank" href="https://caiso.regfox.com/interconnection-customer-user-group-march-18-2025" rel="noreferrer noopener"><i><strong>Interconnection Customer User Group Registration Link</strong></i></a></p><p><strong>Notice - </strong><a target="_blank" href="https://www.caiso.com/notices/interconnection-customer-user-group-call-3-18-25" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://www.caiso.com/notices/interconnection-customer-user-group-call-3-18-25</a></p></div><div><p>Yelena Kopylov-alford, <a href="mailto:ykopylovalford@caiso.com">ykopylovalford@caiso.com</a></p></div><div><p><a href="https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/interconnection-customer-user-group-mar-17-2026-0100-pm" target="_blank">View more information on this event and its related documents.</a></p></div></body></html>
URL:https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/interconnection-customer-user-group-mar-17-2026-0100-pm
DTSTAMP:20251219T011200Z
END:VEVENT
