UID:221611@caiso.com
DTSTART:20260212T170000Z
DTEND:20260212T200000Z
SUMMARY:Financial Planning Initiatives (including Start-up Funding for the Regional Organization for Western Energy) - Straw Proposal
DESCRIPTION:The California ISO is launching a new initiative on the Financial Planning Initiatives (including Start-up Funding for the Regional Organization for Western Energy) and will host a public stakeholder call on Feb. 12, 2026. \nThis multi-topic finance initiative encompasses critical funding and planning actions such as extending the next Financial Planning Initiatives (including Start-up Funding for the Regional Organization for Western Energy). Together, these requests support long-term financial sustainability and maintain rate alignment with evolving cost and operational needs.\nA straw proposal will be posted a week ahead of the meeting. The presentation will be available on the initiative webpage prior to the call.\nCategories\nLegal and regulatoryMarketsOperationsWeb and audio participation information\nStep 1: join web conference at https://intellor.webex.com/intellor/j.php?MTID=m61a5c95add0888634edbf3246acfe494 \nStep 2: connect audio by selecting computer audio or selecting call me and enter your phone number\nAudio only participation: call 1-844-621-3956, access code: 25358170159\nTechnical support: call Intellor at 1-301-250-7202\nRelated information\nMeeting notice - https://www.caiso.com/notices/financial-planning-initiatives-straw-proposal-posted-call-on-2-12-26 \n\nYelena Kopylov-Alford, ykopylovalford@caiso.com \n\nView more information on this event and its related documents: https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/financial-planning-initiatives-including-start-up-funding-for-the-regional-organization-for-western-energy-straw-proposal-feb-12-2026-0900-am
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body lang="EN-US" link="#0072BC" vlink="#03519A" style="font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;" ><div><p>The California ISO is launching a new initiative on the Financial Planning Initiatives (including Start-up Funding for the Regional Organization for Western Energy) and will host a public stakeholder call on Feb. 12, 2026.  </p><p>This multi-topic finance initiative encompasses critical funding and planning actions such as extending the next Financial Planning Initiatives (including Start-up Funding for the Regional Organization for Western Energy). Together, these requests support long-term financial sustainability and maintain rate alignment with evolving cost and operational needs.</p><p>A straw proposal will be posted a week ahead of the meeting. The presentation will be available on the <a target="_blank" href="https://stakeholdercenter.caiso.com/StakeholderInitiatives/financial-planning-initiatives-and-regional-organization-start-up-funding" rel="noreferrer noopener">initiative webpage</a> prior to the call.</p><p style="margin-left:0in;"><strong>Categories</strong></p><ul><li>Legal and regulatory</li><li>Markets</li><li>Operations</li></ul><p style="margin-left:0in;"><strong>Web and audio participation information</strong></p><p>Step 1: join web conference at <a target="_blank" href="https://intellor.webex.com/intellor/j.php?MTID=m61a5c95add0888634edbf3246acfe494" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://intellor.webex.com/intellor/j.php?MTID=m61a5c95add0888634edbf3246acfe494</a></p><p>Step 2: connect audio by selecting <i>computer audio</i> or selecting <i>call me</i> and enter your phone number</p><p>Audio only participation: call 1-844-621-3956, access code: 25358170159</p><p>Technical support: call  Intellor  at 1-301-250-7202</p><p><strong>Related information</strong></p><p><strong>Meeting notice -</strong><a target="_blank" href="https://www.caiso.com/notices/financial-planning-initiatives-straw-proposal-posted-call-on-2-12-26" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://www.caiso.com/notices/financial-planning-initiatives-straw-proposal-posted-call-on-2-12-26</a></p></div><div><p>Yelena Kopylov-Alford, <a href="mailto:ykopylovalford@caiso.com">ykopylovalford@caiso.com</a></p></div><div><p><a href="https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/financial-planning-initiatives-including-start-up-funding-for-the-regional-organization-for-western-energy-straw-proposal-feb-12-2026-0900-am" target="_blank">View more information on this event and its related documents.</a></p></div></body></html>
URL:https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/financial-planning-initiatives-including-start-up-funding-for-the-regional-organization-for-western-energy-straw-proposal-feb-12-2026-0900-am
DTSTAMP:20260121T192600Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:221743@caiso.com
DTSTART:20260211T210000Z
DTEND:20260211T230000Z
SUMMARY:Extended Day-Ahead Market (EDAM) Training for Intertie Scheduling Readiness
DESCRIPTION:What topics will be covered?   \nThe California ISO (CAISO) will host a training webinar on February 11, 2026, to provide an overview of the changes to intertie scheduling and modeling associated with the Extended Day-Ahead Market (EDAM) go-live.\nDuring this session, the CAISO customer readiness and training team will host a training session illustrating what remains the same and what is changing in relation to intertie schedules and modeling on CAISO interties with EDAM, WEIM, and non-market balancing areas across a transitional period.  The training session will include discussion of scheduling of RA imports across the different interties and reassignment functionality applicable in limited instances for RA imports.   \nWho should attend?\nThis training is intended for Scheduling Coordinators operating within the CAISO Balancing Authority Area, entities planning to participate in EDAM, and anyone involved in Western energy markets who would like to stay informed.\nWeb and audio participation information\nStep 1: join web conference at https://caiso.webex.com/caiso/j.php?MTID=m473a4398c06ca075f4e9e2c72b582a8e \nStep 2: connect audio by selecting computer audio or selecting call me and enter your phone number\nAudio only participation: call 1-844-621-3956, access code: 2497 057 1664\nTechnical support: call Intellor at 1-301-250-7202\nRelated information\nhttps://stakeholdercenter.caiso.com/StakeholderInitiatives/Extended-day-ahead-market \n\nCustomerReadiness@Caiso.com \n\nView more information on this event and its related documents: https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/extended-day-ahead-market-edam-training-for-intertie-scheduling-readiness-feb-11-2026-0100-pm
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body lang="EN-US" link="#0072BC" vlink="#03519A" style="font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;" ><div><p style="margin-left:0in;"><strong>What topics will be covered?     </strong></p><p style="margin-left:0.25pt;">The California ISO (CAISO) will host a training webinar on February 11, 2026, to provide an overview of the changes to intertie scheduling and modeling associated with the Extended Day-Ahead Market (EDAM) go-live.</p><p style="margin-left:0.25pt;">During this session, the CAISO customer readiness and training team will host a training session illustrating what remains the same and what is changing in relation to intertie schedules and modeling on CAISO interties with EDAM, WEIM, and non-market balancing areas across a transitional period.   The training session will include discussion of scheduling of RA imports across the different interties and reassignment functionality applicable in limited instances for RA imports.     </p><p style="margin-left:0in;"><strong>Who should attend?</strong></p><p style="margin-left:0.25pt;">This training is intended for Scheduling Coordinators operating within the CAISO Balancing Authority Area, entities planning to participate in EDAM, and anyone involved in Western energy markets who would like to stay informed.</p><p style="margin-left:0in;"><strong>Web and audio participation information</strong></p><p>Step 1: join web conference at <a target="_blank" href="https://caiso.webex.com/caiso/j.php?MTID=m473a4398c06ca075f4e9e2c72b582a8e" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://caiso.webex.com/caiso/j.php?MTID=m473a4398c06ca075f4e9e2c72b582a8e</a></p><p>Step 2: connect audio by selecting <i>computer audio</i> or selecting <i>call me</i> and enter your phone number</p><p>Audio only participation: call 1-844-621-3956, access code: 2497 057 1664</p><p>Technical support: call  Intellor  at 1-301-250-7202</p><p><strong>Related information</strong></p><p><a target="_blank" href="https://stakeholdercenter.caiso.com/StakeholderInitiatives/Extended-day-ahead-market" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://stakeholdercenter.caiso.com/StakeholderInitiatives/Extended-day-ahead-market</a></p></div><div><p><a href="mailto:CustomerReadiness@Caiso.com">CustomerReadiness@Caiso.com</a></p></div><div><p><a href="https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/extended-day-ahead-market-edam-training-for-intertie-scheduling-readiness-feb-11-2026-0100-pm" target="_blank">View more information on this event and its related documents.</a></p></div></body></html>
URL:https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/extended-day-ahead-market-edam-training-for-intertie-scheduling-readiness-feb-11-2026-0100-pm
DTSTAMP:20260123T204100Z
END:VEVENT
