SUMMARY:Stakeholder Workshop - Assembly Bill 825 - California Job Study
DESCRIPTION:What topics will be covered?\nOverview of Assembly Bill (AB) 825 requirements for the job study and its objectives\nReview of the study&#039;s scope and methodology\nDiscussion of preliminary assumptions, inputs, and analytical approachSeeking stakeholder feedback and discussionCategories\nMarkets\nWeb and audio participation information\nStep 1: join web conference at https://intellor.webex.com/intellor/j.php?MTID=m034e59cb83d32cf836707cc885cf0ead \nStep 2: connect audio by selecting computer audio or selecting call me and enter your phone number\nAudio only participation: call 1-650-479-3208, access code: 25358548708\nTechnical support: call Intellor at 1-301-250-7202\nRelated information\nhttps://www.westernenergymarkets.com/pathways-implementation-policy-initiatives \n\nChristina Guimera, cguimera@caiso.com \n\nView more information on this event and its related documents: https://www.caiso.com/meetings-events/calendar/stakeholder-workshop-assembly-bill-825-california-job-study-jun-09-2026-0900-am
